//! The S4 wire seam (spike memo Q3, decision 2): every state-machine
//! step of the authentication adapter driven hermetically through the
//! REAL Muon hyper transport against a hand-written std HTTP/1.1
//! responder on loopback, pointed at by a custom `Environment`
//! (`Scheme::Http` skips TLS). The login steps run a REAL SRP exchange
//! in both directions: the client proof is generated by pinned
//! `proton-srp` client code and verified by a real `proton-srp` server
//! interaction (muon's own SRP implementation, driving the same
//! verifier the scripted API would store), and the server proof it
//! returns is verified by the client — no canned SRP bytes anywhere.
//!
//! Recorded limit (spike memo Q3): DoH-based indirect resolution cannot
//! be loopback-faked, so alternative-routing coverage exercises the
//! direct-class multi-server partition (`find_available_sender`'s
//! ordering across a dead and a live direct server) — the same code
//! path AR uses. DoH/indirect resolution and TLS pinning have no
//! automated offline coverage; tracked for a pre-release networked arm
//! (the canary arm below is direct-only too).
//!
//! The canary arm at the bottom is the S1 harness's real-muon emitter
//! (m2-plan S1/S4): muon's REAL auth code paths driven offline with the
//! canary values as live credentials, asserted through
//! `protonwire_core::redact::canary::assert_no_secrets_reach_logs`
//! unchanged.

